tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-251-an-escape-by-code-writes-only-what-a-line-cannot-show.hero:24:13: error[escape_not_needed]: `\u{200b}` writes the invisible character U+200B, which a string holds as itself: `\u{…}` writes only a control character, a bidirectional control, U+2028 or U+2029
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-251-an-escape-by-code-writes-only-what-a-line-cannot-show.hero:27:13: error[nul_in_string]: `\u{0}` writes a NUL, and no escape writes one: a NUL is a byte no screen shows, so a `str` that must hold one is built from bytes as the program runs, a `[u8]` read by `validated_bytes()`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-251-an-escape-by-code-writes-only-what-a-line-cannot-show.hero:30:12: error[unknown_escape]: `\u{d800}` is not an escape sequence — it names no character, and a string writes by its code only a control character, a bidirectional control, U+2028 or U+2029, as `\u{1b}`, in lowercase hexadecimal; write `\\` for a literal backslash
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-251-an-escape-by-code-writes-only-what-a-line-cannot-show.hero:30:20: error[unknown_escape]: `\u{110000}` is not an escape sequence — it names no character, and a string writes by its code only a control character, a bidirectional control, U+2028 or U+2029, as `\u{1b}`, in lowercase hexadecimal; write `\\` for a literal backslash
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-251-an-escape-by-code-writes-only-what-a-line-cannot-show.hero:30:30: error[unknown_escape]: `\u{}` is not an escape sequence — it names no character, and a string writes by its code only a control character, a bidirectional control, U+2028 or U+2029, as `\u{1b}`, in lowercase hexadecimal; write `\\` for a literal backslash
